.TH SDL_TimeFromWindows 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_TimeFromWindows \- Converts a Windows FILETIME (100-nanosecond intervals since January 1, 1601) to an SDL time.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_time.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Time SDL_TimeFromWindows(Uint32 dwLowDateTime, Uint32 dwHighDateTime);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function takes the two 32-bit values of the FILETIME structure as parameters\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I dwLowDateTime
the low portion of the Windows FILETIME value\[char46]
.TP
.I dwHighDateTime
the high portion of the Windows FILETIME value\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the converted SDL time\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

